            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tabpanel" id="panel-build" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-build" tabindex="0" hidden>
          <div class="tab-copy">
            <h3>You accept every edit</h3>
            <p>Each change arrives as a real diff you review hunk by hunk. Accept, always-allow or decline &mdash; and it is saved with a backup before anything lands.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tab-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="mini-diff lg">
              <div class="d-line del"><span class="d-g">&minus;</span>export function parse(s) {</div>
              <div class="d-line add"><span class="d-g">+</span>export function parse(s) {</div>
              <div class="d-line add"><span class="d-g">+</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;try { return JSON.parse(s) }</div>
              <div class="d-bar"><span class="d-pri">Accept</span><span>Always</span><span>Decline</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tabpanel" id="panel-auto" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-auto" tabindex="0" hidden>
          <div class="tab-copy">
            <h3>Edits apply immediately</h3>
            <p>For the ones who already trust it: writes land straight away, still snapshotted first. <code>/undo</code> reverts the batch, <code>/history</code> goes further back.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tab-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="mini-applied">
              <span class="ok-dot">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>src/api/fetch.ts</strong>
                <span>backup written &middot; <code>/undo</code> reverts</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
